  "limitations_and_boundaries": [
    "The method assumes linearity, no unobserved confounders, and non-Gaussian disturbance variables.",
    "It is never possible to completely confirm the assumptions purely from observational data; controlled experiments are needed for verification.",
    "Only pathological cases constructed by mischievous data designers seem likely to be problematic.",
    "The real data examples reported are rather limited.",
    "The practical value needs further determination by applying to more real-world data sets and comparing to other methods."
